{
    "background_story": "Chana was a young Andean woman who lived in the mountains of Peru. She was a skilled weaver and storyteller, known for her vibrant textiles and rich knowledge of local legends. One day, while out gathering plants, Chana stumbled upon a hidden glacial lake, known as Huainaputina, which was said to possess mystical powers. As she approached the lake's crystal-clear waters, she felt an intense energy and connection to the land. From that moment on, Chana became a guardian of the lake, protecting it from harm and sharing its secrets with her community. Her deep respect and care for the natural world earned her the title of 'Kamayuq', or lake keeper, and her legacy lived on through the stories and traditions she passed down to her people.",
